findings.body:
A failure here leaves a failing "Review with Claude" check on the PR head. Causes include:
- the OAuth token's usage limit (the same budget-exhaustion case this backup exists for);
- the 15-minute job timeout on a large diff;
- an API error, or no `structured_output`;
- the action's write-permission check refusing a triage-only user who added the label.

As the header comment says, a failed check leaves the PR UNSTABLE, which PR Auto-Merge never merges, even at the review cap. So a failing backup reviewer blocks a PR that Copilot has already reviewed, until someone pushes again or re-adds the label.

Fix:
- Add `continue-on-error: true` to this step and emit a `::warning::` instead.
- Have the post job run only when the step succeeded and produced output, e.g. add an `ok` output set from `steps.claude.outcome == 'success' && steps.claude.outputs.structured_output != ''`.
